Context: T146 measurement vehicles. Design choices: the relay shape models what the sync protocol actually sees over DERP (one rate-limited connection per agent, one batch in flight per source, per-exchange RTT), not the DERP internals; validation is that the plain extrapolation lands just above the measured 3-hour baseline. The dictionary trains through the zstd CLI on 64 KiB chunks of train-half sections and measures whole-file sections (the wire unit); sessions are sampled systematically (every Nth by id) because largest-first sampling is tail-biased toward huge files that compress best. The local bench reads upload_payload_bytes/upload_wire_bytes from the join child's final observe snapshot - SIGTERM stop publishes it - and per-side CPU from /proc, so the A/B never trusts the harness's own accounting.
